---
import Slide from '@decks/templates/Slide.astro';

// The differentiating slide, and it is about something that already
// exists rather than something promised. The param vocabulary is
// machine-readable by construction, so the claim is demonstrable: every
// decision has a URL that opens the component in exactly that state.
//
// If this needs an image later, the entry page is the artifact to shoot:
// /decks/2026-checklist-component/prototypes/

const properties = [
	['Named values only', 'Never a free-form string.'],
	['Unknown values ignored', 'Never guessed at.'],
	['One URL per decision', 'Opens the component in exactly that state.'],
];
---

<Slide subtitle="Docs → For the agent reading it">
	<div class="grid gap-9">
		<div class="text-strong max-w-[1500px] text-5xl">
			Increasingly the thing reading a component doc is an agent writing the
			implementation.
		</div>
		<div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-7">
			{
				properties.map(([what, why]) => (
					<div>
						<div class="text-strong text-3xl font-medium">{what}</div>
						<div class="text-subdued mt-2 text-xl">{why}</div>
					</div>
				))
			}
		</div>
		<div class="text-subdued text-3xl">
			So a ticket, a doc, or a model can point at one configuration and
			<span class="text-strong">mean precisely one thing.</span>
		</div>
	</div>
</Slide>
